    "dynamic_instructions": "{\r\n  \"datasetView\": \"**Find the Problem**\\n\\nGoal: Find what in the data made Tree 1 get records wrong.\\n\\n1. In **Predict**, choose your label from **My Data** in your guide. In **Using**, choose only the two features from **Tree 1** in your guide. Click **Train model**.\\n2. Go to the **Testing** tab. Do steps a and b there.\\n3. Come back to this tab. Do steps c and d:\\n    - c. Click one feature at a time to open Column Analysis. Find the feature whose Least Common category has the fewest records. Write that feature, its Least Common category and how many records it has in **Find the Problem** in your guide.\\n    - d. Click **Filter**. Choose that category. Write how many records are in each category of your label.\\n\\nYou are done when **Find the Problem** in your guide is full.\",\r\n  \"results\": \"**Find the Problem**\\n\\nGoal: Find what in the data made Tree 1 get records wrong.\\n\\n- a. Click **Accuracy**. Then click **Incorrect**. Write the **Incorrect** number in **Find the Problem** in your guide. Add **Correct** and **Incorrect**. Write the total as the test records.\\n- b. Click **Expand columns**. Look at one feature at a time in the incorrect records. Write the category that shows up in most of them. If no category shows up most, write \\\"none\\\".\\n\\nThen go back to the **Dataset** tab for steps c and d.\"\r\n}",
